{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/240811-flesh-changeling-2nd-edition-and-is-too-much-of-it-bad","id":240811,"title":"\"Flesh,\" Changeling 2nd Edition ... and is too much of it bad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-25T15:33:14-07:00","id":240811,"title":"\"Flesh,\" Changeling 2nd Edition ... and is too much of it bad?","content":"So, I have noticed that the word &quot;flesh&quot; has been thrown around a bit since the announcement of the second edition of Changeling. From the original title of the project (&quot;Too Much Flesh&quot;) to various enigmatic comments from the game's developer.<br /> <br /> The word is very evocative and not commonly used, which makes me feel as if its inclusion in discussions about the game is purposeful.<br /> <br /> What do you think &quot;Flesh&quot; is ... in context of the upcoming revision? Is it a new trait? Just a fluff thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T15:45:08-07:00","id":240838,"title":"","content":"&quot;This too solid flesh&quot;, not &quot;too much flesh&quot;. It's a Shakespeare quote. I don't remember what the context is in the play, but off the cuff it brings to mind a feeling of being trapped, which you could see both ways: a Changeling who can't escape what they've become, or someone who seeks the wonders of the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> I don't remember seeing it particularly often, but I'm pretty sure it's just fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T15:48:36-07:00","id":240842,"title":"","content":"\u2026&quot;Too <b>Solid</b> Flesh&quot; is a <i>Hamlet </i>quote from the soliloquy that gave us &quot;Frailty, thy name is woman!&quot; in the context of the title character being anguished at the speed of his mother's remarriage and moving on from the death of her late husband. The entire speech revolves around how awful Hamlet finds the state of affairs that demonstrate how terribly mutable life is and how painful it is to remember how different things uses to be. &quot;O, that this too too solid flesh would melt, thaw and resolve into a dew!&quot; is followed immediately by the alternative wish of &quot;Or if I could just kill myself without being sent to Hell thereafter!&quot;<br /> <br /> Changelings are traumatized survivors of a stint as the plaything of a cruel and protean Fate and only managed to get home because the things they remembered hadn't dramatically changed in the stretched span of time they were gone. There's no Twilight in the Hedge and the fae have a number of parallels to various ephemeral beings, many of whom view the primary attraction of the material world as &quot;it is a place with fleshy beings of various fun and profitable uses.&quot;<br /> <br /> A picture hardly need be painted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T03:13:53-07:00","id":241198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/240811-flesh-changeling-2nd-edition-and-is-too-much-of-it-bad?p=240842#post240842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026&quot;Too <b>Solid</b> Flesh&quot; is a <i>Hamlet </i>quote from the soliloquy that gave us &quot;Frailty, thy name is woman!&quot; in the context of the title character being anguished at the speed of his mother's remarriage and moving on from the death of her late husband. The entire speech revolves around how awful Hamlet finds the state of affairs that demonstrate how terribly mutable life is and how painful it is to remember how different things uses to be. &quot;O, that this too too solid flesh would melt, thaw and resolve into a dew!&quot; is followed immediately by the alternative wish of &quot;Or if I could just kill myself without being sent to Hell thereafter!&quot;<br /> <br /> Changelings are traumatized survivors of a stint as the plaything of a cruel and protean Fate and only managed to get home because the things they remembered hadn't dramatically changed in the stretched span of time they were gone. There's no Twilight in the Hedge and the fae have a number of parallels to various ephemeral beings, many of whom view the primary attraction of the material world as &quot;it is a place with fleshy beings of various fun and profitable uses.&quot;<br /> <br /> A picture hardly need be painted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read the OP, and I was all, &quot;Man. That totally needs an answer. Let's see...&quot; <br /> <br /> I start formulating a response, and you drop that. <br /> <br /> Spot on take on the Hamlet reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}